INT. DENTIST WAITING ROOM - DAY

Beige chairs. A fish tank. A bowl of lollipops marked FOR GOOD PATIENTS ONLY.

A CLOWN in full costume sits stiffly with a balloon animal. DR. PATRICIA VOSS, the dentist, in a mask, hovers by the door. DEEDEE, her receptionist, types. A little boy, MILO, six, wails in his mother's lap. His mother, JUANITA, bounces him.

DEEDEE
Mr. Clown? You're next.

CLOWN
I'm not a patient. I'm the entertainment.

DR. VOSS
We didn't book entertainment.

CLOWN
Somebody did. Under "Gus."

DEEDEE
Gus?

CLOWN
That's me. Gus the Clown.

GUS
(tapping his nose)
Honk.

MILO shrieks. Juanita clamps her hand over his mouth. Dr. Voss and Deedee both lunge for the lollipops. The three adults collide at the bowl, sending lollipops flying; Gus slips, his balloon dog squeaks, and the fish tank sloshes.

Milo stops crying. He stares at Gus.

MILO
Do the dog again.

Gus, flat on the floor, honks.
